{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Decision (operator, 2026-08-30): Option B approved — add a dedicated `expression_unresolved` code\n\n`ExpressionError` (execute-time workflow expression-resolution failure: unset input, missing\nstep output, loop var out of scope, unresolvable `${{ }}`, missing secret/env) will map to a\nnew **`expression_unresolved`** code, NOT `llm_unavailable` (misleading — asserts an outage)\nand NOT `command_failed` (accurate but too vague to guide an agent's retry-vs-fix decision on\nthe `run_workflow` surface).\n\n**Rationale / precedent.** gRPC canonical status codes reserve `UNAVAILABLE` for transient\noutages and give caller/state faults specific codes, explicitly warning against dumping a\nclassifiable fault into the generic `UNKNOWN`/`INTERNAL` bucket (= our `command_failed`).\nHTTP's 4xx-vs-5xx split says the same. `invalid_input` was rejected: `ExpressionError` also\nfires for environment faults (missing secret, empty upstream output), so \"invalid input\" would\nbe a *different* misleading code.\n\n**Implementation shape (low blast radius):**\n- Set `error_code = \"expression_unresolved\"` as an attribute on `ExpressionError` (or\n  `WorkflowError` if the whole family fits) so `error_code_for` branch 5 (explicit\n  `error_code`) fires BEFORE branch 6 (`LLMError → llm_unavailable`). Only `ExpressionError`\n  changes; other `LLMError`s untouched.\n- Add `expression_unresolved` to `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`) + the guardrail\n  contract test `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_error_code_taxonomy_contract.py`.\n- Tests through the REAL `run_workflow`/execute surface (per AC): a genuine execute-time LLM\n  outage still returns `llm_unavailable`; an `ExpressionError` returns `expression_unresolved`.\n\n**Separate follow-up (not this ticket):** narrow `error_code_for` branch 6 to fire\n`llm_unavailable` only for `LLMUnavailableError` (reserve it for true outages) — a broader\ncleanup with its own blast radius (sweep all `LLMError` subclasses). File discovered_from this\nticket when implemented.\n\nOrigin unchanged: 8a31 (blanket LLMError→llm_unavailable). Ready to move from\nescalate/design-decision to ready-to-fix."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788108886242336453,"uuid":"8f0ded43-cb2f-41ea-b507-b4e0a116eaa4"}